{"name":"Soul Train","hex":"#58475e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soul","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spirit or essence of a person usually thought to consist of one's thoughts and personality, often believed to live on after the person's death.","The spirit or essence of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characteristic of or pertaining to African American culture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul"},{"term":"train","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Elongated or trailing portion.","A trail or line of something, especially gunpowder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To practice an ability.","To teach and form (someone) by practice; to educate (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soul Train","blocks":[{"text":"Soul Train is an American musical variety television show. After airing locally on WCIU-TV in Chicago, Illinois, for a year, the popular series then aired nationally in syndication from October 2, 1971, to March 25, 2006. In its 35-year history, the show primarily featured performances by R&B, soul, and hip-hop artists. The series was created by Don Cornelius, who also served as its first and longest-serving host and executive producer."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Soul_Train.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_Train","wikidata":"Q195732"},{"title":"Soul","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, the soul is the immaterial aspect or essence of a living being. It is typically believed to be immortal and to exist apart from the material world. Anthropologists and psychologists have found that most humans believe in the existence of a soul or spirit, and that they have cross-culturally distinguished between the soul and the material body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg/330px-Schiavonetti_Soul_leaving_body_1808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul","wikidata":"Q9165"},{"title":"Train","blocks":[{"text":"A train is a series of connected vehicles that run along a railway track and transport people or freight. Trains are typically pulled or pushed by locomotives, though some are self-propelled, such as multiple units or railcars. Passengers and cargo are carried in railroad cars, also known as wagons or carriages. Trains are designed to a certain gauge, or distance between rails. Most trains operate on steel tracks with steel wheels, the low friction of which makes them more efficient than other forms of transport. Many countries use rail transport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B7%D0%B4_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%84%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8B_%D0%A8%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%89%D0%B5._%D0%92%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B6%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C.jpg/330px-%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B7%D0%B4_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%84%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8B_%D0%A8%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%89%D0%B5._%D0%92%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B6%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Train","wikidata":"Q870"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Soul_Train.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Soul_Train.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoul_Train.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Staple_Singers_on_Soul_Train.jpg/500px-Staple_Singers_on_Soul_Train.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Staple_Singers_on_Soul_Train.jpg/500px-Staple_Singers_on_Soul_Train.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cornelius (second from right) with The Staple Singers in 1974","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStaple_Singers_on_Soul_Train.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Criminal_Minds_at_Paley_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Criminal_Minds_at_Paley_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Criminal_Minds_at_Paley_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Criminal_Minds_at_Paley_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Criminal_Minds_at_Paley_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shemar Moore hosted Soul Train from 2000 to 2003.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACriminal_Minds_at_Paley_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Dorian_Gregory_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Dorian_Gregory_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Dorian_Gregory_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Dorian_Gregory_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Dorian_Gregory_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dorian Gregory hosted Soul Train from 2003 to 2006.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADorian_Gregory_(cropped)